1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Ploby keeps an AI purchasing agent inside a client-funded project budget.
Monad testnet demo: role approvals use demo signatures.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The contractor gives a task and selects vendor documents.
Kiln qwen3-32b makes the plan; the agent can only request purchases.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The 40-image offer exceeds the KRW 200,000 cap after VAT.
The agent follows its next planned option: 10 images for KRW 55,000.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The domain is approved. The unlisted keyboard vendor is blocked.
Every request keeps its decision and rule.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Approval reserves funds; it does not mean the expense is paid.
The contractor reports the purchase and submits a receipt.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The receipt is read and matched to the commitment.
The client reviews KRW 24,200 before approving settlement.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The client approves payment to the fixed contractor wallet.
The escrow settles 24,200 TestKRW on Monad testnet.

8
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:21,000
This is the confirmed settlement transaction.
The transfer and the log refer to the same completed payment.

9
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Track B boundary run 1: same policy, fresh project.
Request an office keyboard from an unlisted vendor.

10
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:42,000
The live plan requests the keyboard. The engine returns BLOCK: Vendor.
No funds are reserved, and the stopped request is recorded.

11
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Track B boundary run 2: request the 40-image pack.
Its total includes VAT: KRW 203,500.

12
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
BLOCK: Per-purchase limit. The total exceeds KRW 200,000.
No alternative was selected, so this run makes no purchase.

13
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Both stops appear in the audit with their log lines.
Each has a matching Decided event on the public chain.

14
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:16,000
The client can also pause new commitments.
The next task records a block and stops its remaining requests.

15
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:24,000
The paused task ends after its first blocked request.
Accepted commitments remain eligible for receipt review and settlement.

16
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The exported workflow snapshot has 31 entries and 13 matching chain calls.
Its five original documents match their recorded hashes.

17
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:41,000
The verifier reconstructs the payment from the log, originals and public chain.
Human approval remains partial in this demo because its signatures are demo keys.

18
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Eight matched document reads: 8/8 expected outcomes in each arm.
Energy is an explicit hardware estimate; no Kiln power telemetry is claimed.
